WEBVTT


00:00:19.044 --> 00:00:22.104
<i>Hold on 'cause I'm letting go</i>


00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.716
<i>I'm gonna lasso your heart like a rodeo</i>


00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:29.547
<i>I'm gonna give you some
Till you want some more</i>


00:00:29.721 --> 00:00:33.452
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:37.425
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:37.595 --> 00:00:41.190
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:41.366 --> 00:00:44.927
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:45.103 --> 00:00:48.630
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:48.807 --> 00:00:52.174
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:55.609
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.477
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:00:59.651 --> 00:01:03.678
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:07.450
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:10.753
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:10.929 --> 00:01:14.695
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:17.858
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:21.528
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:24.971
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:25.143 --> 00:01:27.168
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:28.613 --> 00:01:31.446
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:36.514
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:39.987
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:40.158 --> 00:01:42.092
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:17.195 --> 00:02:20.756
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:22.092
You have an appointment...


00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.861
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:25.036 --> 00:02:27.971
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:28.139 --> 00:02:30.198
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:30.375 --> 00:02:31.899
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:32.343 --> 00:02:34.174
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:34.345 --> 00:02:36.176
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:37.740
Bath. Now.


00:02:38.716 --> 00:02:40.581
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:43.181
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:46.758 --> 00:02:48.851
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:49.027 --> 00:02:51.621
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:02:51.796 --> 00:02:54.230
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:07.712 --> 00:03:09.145
Victor, no.


00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.754
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:17.922 --> 00:03:23.918
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:24.395 --> 00:03:26.920
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:27.632 --> 00:03:29.327
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:30.835 --> 00:03:32.427
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:32.971 --> 00:03:34.336
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:37.134
Nothing.


00:03:41.779 --> 00:03:44.646
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:44.816 --> 00:03:46.181
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:48.987 --> 00:03:52.013
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.421
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:03:55.593 --> 00:03:59.051
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.324
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.161
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:04.335 --> 00:04:06.530
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:06.704 --> 00:04:10.162
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:11.843 --> 00:04:14.107
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:16.975
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:17.148 --> 00:04:20.242
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:20.418 --> 00:04:21.908
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:22.086 --> 00:04:24.646
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:24.822 --> 00:04:26.619
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:40.171 --> 00:04:44.130
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:44.309 --> 00:04:47.676
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:47.845 --> 00:04:49.710
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:04:49.881 --> 00:04:52.315
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:04:52.483 --> 00:04:56.010
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:04:56.187 --> 00:04:59.748
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:00.258 --> 00:05:05.161
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.161
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:07.665 --> 00:05:11.658
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:15.139 --> 00:05:17.471
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:17.942 --> 00:05:23.005
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:23.314 --> 00:05:26.442
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:29.678
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:31.356 --> 00:05:33.620
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:37.227
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.724
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:41.899 --> 00:05:43.730
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:45.003 --> 00:05:48.200
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:48.373 --> 00:05:52.139
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.971
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:56.909
That record was amazing.


00:05:57.081 --> 00:06:00.050
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:01.552 --> 00:06:04.020
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:04.188 --> 00:06:07.089
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:07.258 --> 00:06:08.919
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:10.461 --> 00:06:16.024
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.361
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:18.536 --> 00:06:21.903
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:22.073 --> 00:06:24.234
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:26.775
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:26.944 --> 00:06:30.846
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:31.983 --> 00:06:34.076
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:34.585 --> 00:06:36.951
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:37.522 --> 00:06:39.649
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:39.824 --> 00:06:41.792
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:41.959 --> 00:06:43.950
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:44.128 --> 00:06:47.097
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:47.532 --> 00:06:50.296
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:06:50.468 --> 00:06:53.369
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:55.369
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:58.407
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:06:58.576 --> 00:07:01.204
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.670
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:03.848 --> 00:07:05.440
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:05.616 --> 00:07:07.982
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:08.152 --> 00:07:11.553
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:12.156 --> 00:07:17.560
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:26.437 --> 00:07:28.132
Watch out.


00:07:28.606 --> 00:07:30.631
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:31.642 --> 00:07:35.237
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:35.413 --> 00:07:37.210
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:37.381 --> 00:07:39.747
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:39.917 --> 00:07:41.282
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:41.452 --> 00:07:44.444
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:44.622 --> 00:07:48.581
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.489
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:07:51.329 --> 00:07:53.229
You giving our ball back or what?


00:07:53.397 --> 00:07:57.026
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:01.839 --> 00:08:05.104
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:07.445 --> 00:08:11.176
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:11.349 --> 00:08:12.714
Hotter.


00:08:12.884 --> 00:08:14.511
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:14.685 --> 00:08:16.915
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:17.088 --> 00:08:19.648
First time for everything, right?


00:08:26.798 --> 00:08:28.493
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:28.666 --> 00:08:29.894
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:30.368 --> 00:08:33.428
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:33.604 --> 00:08:35.799
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:35.973 --> 00:08:39.431
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.874
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:42.046 --> 00:08:45.413
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:45.683 --> 00:08:48.015
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:48.186 --> 00:08:49.710
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:08:49.887 --> 00:08:52.788
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:08:52.957 --> 00:08:56.393
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:08:56.561 --> 00:09:00.088
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:00.264 --> 00:09:05.429
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:05.603 --> 00:09:09.164
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.433
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:11.609 --> 00:09:14.510
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.806
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:16.981 --> 00:09:20.007
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:20.184 --> 00:09:22.379
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:30.928 --> 00:09:32.190
Whoa.


00:09:32.363 --> 00:09:35.457
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:35.633 --> 00:09:38.295
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:38.469 --> 00:09:39.629
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:39.804 --> 00:09:43.205
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:43.374 --> 00:09:45.035
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:45.209 --> 00:09:46.233
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.878
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:49.046 --> 00:09:51.446
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:09:51.616 --> 00:09:53.516
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:09:53.684 --> 00:09:55.311
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:09:55.887 --> 00:09:57.980
Om.


00:09:58.789 --> 00:10:01.417
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:01.592 --> 00:10:03.685
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:03.861 --> 00:10:06.386
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:06.764 --> 00:10:08.391
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:09.901 --> 00:10:11.061
My butt is numb.


00:10:11.402 --> 00:10:14.599
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:14.772 --> 00:10:18.230
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:18.409 --> 00:10:21.503
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:21.679 --> 00:10:23.670
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:30.585
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:30.755 --> 00:10:34.316
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:35.192 --> 00:10:38.252
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:38.429 --> 00:10:41.023
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:41.198 --> 00:10:42.495
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:42.667 --> 00:10:45.192
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:45.369 --> 00:10:48.566
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:48.739 --> 00:10:51.173
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:10:51.342 --> 00:10:54.743
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:10:58.516 --> 00:10:59.983
Victor.


00:11:00.151 --> 00:11:05.384
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:29.046 --> 00:11:33.483
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:33.818 --> 00:11:36.309
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:37.355 --> 00:11:40.017
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:40.191 --> 00:11:44.753
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:48.065 --> 00:11:49.089
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:49.266 --> 00:11:51.700
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:11:51.869 --> 00:11:53.461
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:11:53.671 --> 00:11:55.901
Mac and cheese.


00:11:56.807 --> 00:11:59.935
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:00.478 --> 00:12:02.036
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:07.551 --> 00:12:10.918
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:11.088 --> 00:12:14.421
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:15.826 --> 00:12:19.023
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:19.196 --> 00:12:21.289
How did this become my life?


00:12:21.465 --> 00:12:24.457
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:24.635 --> 00:12:26.125
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:26.303 --> 00:12:27.736
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:28.172 --> 00:12:30.367
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:30.541 --> 00:12:32.873
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:38.580
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:40.351 --> 00:12:41.648
Now look at me.


00:12:41.819 --> 00:12:44.310
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:44.488 --> 00:12:47.480
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:47.658 --> 00:12:49.649
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:12:49.827 --> 00:12:52.057
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:12:52.229 --> 00:12:53.992
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:12:55.533 --> 00:12:57.728
Katie, napkin me.


00:12:57.902 --> 00:13:00.393
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:00.805 --> 00:13:04.036
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:04.208 --> 00:13:07.974
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:08.145 --> 00:13:11.774
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:12.716 --> 00:13:15.116
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:15.286 --> 00:13:17.880
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:18.055 --> 00:13:20.922
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:21.092 --> 00:13:22.116
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:22.293 --> 00:13:24.853
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:25.029 --> 00:13:26.963
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:27.131 --> 00:13:30.157
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:30.334 --> 00:13:32.359
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:32.536 --> 00:13:34.504
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:34.672 --> 00:13:35.696
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:35.873 --> 00:13:39.741
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:43.311
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:43.481 --> 00:13:46.575
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:49.048
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.154
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:51.322 --> 00:13:53.552
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:13:53.724 --> 00:13:56.921
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:13:57.094 --> 00:14:01.360
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:01.532 --> 00:14:03.500
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:04.001 --> 00:14:07.528
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:10.074 --> 00:14:15.512
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:15.679 --> 00:14:18.239
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:18.415 --> 00:14:20.508
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:20.684 --> 00:14:22.413
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:22.586 --> 00:14:25.214
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:25.389 --> 00:14:28.722
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:28.893 --> 00:14:30.520
Again.


00:14:30.694 --> 00:14:32.252
Really? Okay.


00:14:32.429 --> 00:14:38.061
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:38.235 --> 00:14:39.361
Ouch.


00:14:39.537 --> 00:14:42.597
I could belch the song better.


00:14:44.208 --> 00:14:46.369
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:46.544 --> 00:14:48.011
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:48.179 --> 00:14:51.080
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:51.248 --> 00:14:55.150
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:14:55.519 --> 00:14:59.182
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:03.394 --> 00:15:05.760
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.659
No.


00:15:07.831 --> 00:15:10.129
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:22.313 --> 00:15:25.612
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:25.783 --> 00:15:28.251
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:38.729 --> 00:15:41.823
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:46.704 --> 00:15:48.433
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:48.606 --> 00:15:49.698
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:49.873 --> 00:15:53.969
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:15:54.144 --> 00:15:55.475
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:15:55.646 --> 00:15:58.410
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:15:58.849 --> 00:16:00.146
Victor!


00:16:00.317 --> 00:16:03.548
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:03.721 --> 00:16:05.882
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:09.393 --> 00:16:11.020
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:20.938 --> 00:16:22.098
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:22.273 --> 00:16:23.672
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:23.841 --> 00:16:27.277
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:27.444 --> 00:16:29.105
Crap.


00:16:32.516 --> 00:16:34.211
This is insane.


00:16:34.385 --> 00:16:38.446
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:48.232 --> 00:16:50.325
You gotta be kidding me.


00:16:52.069 --> 00:16:53.696
Crap.


00:16:57.007 --> 00:17:00.602
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:00.778 --> 00:17:04.578
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:04.748 --> 00:17:06.875
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:07.051 --> 00:17:08.746
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:08.919 --> 00:17:11.479
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:11.655 --> 00:17:14.715
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:14.892 --> 00:17:17.122
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:17.294 --> 00:17:19.421
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:21.765 --> 00:17:23.232
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:29.406 --> 00:17:31.271
Victor.


00:17:35.112 --> 00:17:36.545
Katie?


00:17:37.748 --> 00:17:39.978
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:40.184 --> 00:17:43.449
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.384
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:47.424 --> 00:17:49.255
The truth. Um...


00:17:50.561 --> 00:17:53.894
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:17:54.064 --> 00:17:55.395
Naked.


00:17:56.433 --> 00:17:58.731
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:17:58.902 --> 00:18:00.426
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:02.873 --> 00:18:03.965
There.


00:18:04.141 --> 00:18:07.338
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:11.949 --> 00:18:13.576
I'm kidding.


00:18:14.118 --> 00:18:15.949
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:16.286 --> 00:18:17.310
No, no.


00:18:17.488 --> 00:18:20.889
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:21.058 --> 00:18:23.253
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:23.861 --> 00:18:28.525
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:29.032 --> 00:18:32.832
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:33.003 --> 00:18:35.597
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:39.476 --> 00:18:41.137
What is that?


00:18:41.712 --> 00:18:43.976
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:44.148 --> 00:18:46.116
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:47.317 --> 00:18:49.046
Hey. What...?


00:19:01.899 --> 00:19:04.390
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:04.568 --> 00:19:06.195
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.497
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:08.672 --> 00:19:10.936
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:11.108 --> 00:19:12.132
Do you hear this?


00:19:12.309 --> 00:19:13.970
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:14.144 --> 00:19:15.839
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:16.013 --> 00:19:18.345
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:18.515 --> 00:19:20.710
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:20.884 --> 00:19:22.749
She gave you a CD?


00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:26.287
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:27.524 --> 00:19:31.392
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:32.629 --> 00:19:36.725
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:38.702 --> 00:19:40.897
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:42.039 --> 00:19:43.597
So...


00:19:44.475 --> 00:19:46.602
...that meeting today...


00:19:46.777 --> 00:19:49.575
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:49.913 --> 00:19:51.972
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:19:52.149 --> 00:19:54.583
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:19:54.852 --> 00:19:56.046
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:19:57.521 --> 00:19:59.421
Is it as complicated as me...


00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.718
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:02.993 --> 00:20:06.724
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:11.635 --> 00:20:14.433
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:14.605 --> 00:20:17.665
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:17.841 --> 00:20:20.105
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:24.081 --> 00:20:25.742
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:27.417 --> 00:20:28.714
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:28.886 --> 00:20:31.980
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:32.155 --> 00:20:34.623
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:34.791 --> 00:20:36.952
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:37.127 --> 00:20:38.321
That's interesting.


00:20:38.495 --> 00:20:41.259
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:41.431 --> 00:20:42.659
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:42.833 --> 00:20:44.460
I only have cheese.


00:20:47.638 --> 00:20:49.606
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:49.773 --> 00:20:51.673
Your phone.


00:20:54.711 --> 00:20:57.578
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:20:57.748 --> 00:20:59.306
I have underestimated you.


00:20:59.883 --> 00:21:01.714
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:01.885 --> 00:21:04.979
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:05.155 --> 00:21:07.783
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:07.958 --> 00:21:12.156
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:12.329 --> 00:21:15.594
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:15.766 --> 00:21:19.202
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:19.369 --> 00:21:22.497
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:22.673 --> 00:21:27.804
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:29.079 --> 00:21:31.240
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:36.653 --> 00:21:41.283
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:41.458 --> 00:21:45.554
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:45.729 --> 00:21:49.495
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:49.967 --> 00:21:51.628
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:21:51.802 --> 00:21:53.963
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:21:57.207 --> 00:21:59.903
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:00.477 --> 00:22:03.935
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:04.381 --> 00:22:06.349
I like trouble.


00:22:07.884 --> 00:22:09.010
Hey, kids.


00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:13.756
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:13.924 --> 00:22:16.688
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:20.694
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:20.998 --> 00:22:26.231
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:26.436 --> 00:22:28.904
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:29.172 --> 00:22:31.732
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:31.908 --> 00:22:33.876
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:34.044 --> 00:22:37.104
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:40.340
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:40.517 --> 00:22:43.213
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:43.387 --> 00:22:46.686
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:46.857 --> 00:22:48.688
What if I don't want to?


00:22:49.793 --> 00:22:53.524
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:22:53.697 --> 00:22:55.756
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:22:55.932 --> 00:22:58.196
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:22:58.368 --> 00:23:01.929
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:02.105 --> 00:23:03.595
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:03.774 --> 00:23:05.241
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:06.843 --> 00:23:08.970
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:09.146 --> 00:23:12.274
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:12.683 --> 00:23:16.881
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:17.054 --> 00:23:20.888
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:21.058 --> 00:23:23.959
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:24.127 --> 00:23:26.391
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:26.563 --> 00:23:28.690
You are a star.


00:23:28.865 --> 00:23:33.063
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:33.236 --> 00:23:34.794
I'm a star.


00:23:34.971 --> 00:23:39.135
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:39.309 --> 00:23:41.709
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:41.878 --> 00:23:43.846
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:44.014 --> 00:23:45.572
Every part of him.


00:23:45.749 --> 00:23:49.276
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:49.453 --> 00:23:52.217
And just leave me out of this.


00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:56.050
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:23:56.226 --> 00:23:58.126
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:23:58.729 --> 00:24:00.629
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:00.797 --> 00:24:03.493
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:03.667 --> 00:24:05.726
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:05.902 --> 00:24:07.267
Are we clear?


00:24:07.704 --> 00:24:08.898
Crystal.


00:24:10.841 --> 00:24:13.833
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:18.003
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:18.181 --> 00:24:20.649
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:20.817 --> 00:24:22.148
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:22.319 --> 00:24:24.446
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:24.621 --> 00:24:26.145
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:26.323 --> 00:24:29.690
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:32.556
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:32.729 --> 00:24:34.993
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:35.165 --> 00:24:36.723
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:39.027
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:39.202 --> 00:24:40.669
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:40.837 --> 00:24:43.670
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:46.502
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:46.676 --> 00:24:48.439
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:48.612 --> 00:24:50.307
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:50.747 --> 00:24:53.443
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:24:53.617 --> 00:24:56.347
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:24:56.520 --> 00:24:57.714
We're here to impress.


00:24:57.888 --> 00:25:00.152
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:03.994 --> 00:25:06.462
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:06.630 --> 00:25:08.894
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:09.065 --> 00:25:11.260
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:11.434 --> 00:25:14.801
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:14.971 --> 00:25:17.496
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:17.674 --> 00:25:20.939
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:21.111 --> 00:25:26.413
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:26.583 --> 00:25:33.318
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:34.524 --> 00:25:36.014
That's good.


00:25:43.066 --> 00:25:46.365
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:47.204 --> 00:25:49.536
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:49.706 --> 00:25:51.606
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:25:52.642 --> 00:25:56.237
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:25:56.413 --> 00:25:58.608
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:25:58.782 --> 00:26:00.716
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:00.884 --> 00:26:06.117
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:06.289 --> 00:26:08.484
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:09.025 --> 00:26:10.788
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:10.961 --> 00:26:13.555
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:14.164 --> 00:26:17.463
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:17.634 --> 00:26:19.101
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:19.269 --> 00:26:21.294
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:21.471 --> 00:26:24.463
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:26.643 --> 00:26:29.077
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:32.616 --> 00:26:34.447
Okay.


00:26:35.018 --> 00:26:37.384
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:37.721 --> 00:26:39.484
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:39.656 --> 00:26:41.647
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:41.825 --> 00:26:43.656
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:43.827 --> 00:26:46.125
That I shall not cross.


00:26:46.596 --> 00:26:48.894
So sing something.


00:26:50.567 --> 00:26:52.034
Okay.


00:26:56.172 --> 00:26:58.970
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:26:59.142 --> 00:27:01.633
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:01.811 --> 00:27:03.210
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:03.680 --> 00:27:05.671
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:07.484 --> 00:27:09.952
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:10.120 --> 00:27:12.645
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:12.822 --> 00:27:14.414
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:14.925 --> 00:27:16.552
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:20.495
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:20.664 --> 00:27:22.996
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:23.166 --> 00:27:24.633
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:26.036 --> 00:27:27.697
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:28.638 --> 00:27:31.471
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:31.641 --> 00:27:36.840
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:37.013 --> 00:27:38.571
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:39.683 --> 00:27:42.277
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:42.452 --> 00:27:45.012
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:45.188 --> 00:27:49.557
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:50.961 --> 00:27:53.623
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:27:53.797 --> 00:27:56.061
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:27:56.232 --> 00:27:58.894
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:27:59.069 --> 00:28:01.560
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:06.042 --> 00:28:08.169
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:08.345 --> 00:28:10.973
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:11.147 --> 00:28:14.480
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:14.751 --> 00:28:17.242
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:19.411
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:19.589 --> 00:28:21.887
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:22.058 --> 00:28:23.753
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:24.027 --> 00:28:25.722
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:26.162 --> 00:28:29.996
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:30.467 --> 00:28:34.563
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:34.738 --> 00:28:35.762
...good acoustics.


00:28:36.172 --> 00:28:40.006
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:40.176 --> 00:28:41.768
If you gave them your song.


00:28:43.179 --> 00:28:44.840
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:45.582 --> 00:28:48.278
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:48.451 --> 00:28:49.782
Yeah.


00:28:51.454 --> 00:28:57.984
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:28:58.294 --> 00:28:59.591
You wrote that song today?


00:28:59.763 --> 00:29:03.221
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:03.500 --> 00:29:04.797
You really like this guy.


00:29:04.968 --> 00:29:06.663
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:06.836 --> 00:29:09.031
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:09.205 --> 00:29:12.697
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:14.511 --> 00:29:17.309
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:20.917 --> 00:29:23.750
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:25.789 --> 00:29:28.257
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:28.591 --> 00:29:32.083
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:32.262 --> 00:29:34.287
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:34.464 --> 00:29:35.488
Am not.


00:29:36.533 --> 00:29:39.525
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:39.702 --> 00:29:42.398
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:42.572 --> 00:29:45.132
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:45.308 --> 00:29:48.004
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:48.178 --> 00:29:50.112
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:50.280 --> 00:29:54.307
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:29:54.684 --> 00:29:57.778
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:00.723 --> 00:30:02.247
Okay.


00:30:02.559 --> 00:30:04.151
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:04.327 --> 00:30:05.658
That's my girl.


00:30:05.929 --> 00:30:09.922
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:13.399
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:13.570 --> 00:30:15.333
What? Why?


00:30:15.505 --> 00:30:16.870
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:20.777 --> 00:30:22.335
Katie!


00:30:22.512 --> 00:30:25.948
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:26.116 --> 00:30:27.606
Go.


00:30:27.784 --> 00:30:29.513
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:29.686 --> 00:30:31.017
Angie, heads up.


00:30:32.989 --> 00:30:34.286
Katie!


00:30:39.496 --> 00:30:41.225
What's going on?


00:30:41.397 --> 00:30:42.830
Nothing.


00:30:42.999 --> 00:30:46.127
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:46.302 --> 00:30:48.600
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:48.771 --> 00:30:52.832
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:30:56.079 --> 00:31:00.243
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:00.416 --> 00:31:02.646
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:02.819 --> 00:31:04.252
Oh, no, no.


00:31:04.420 --> 00:31:06.911
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:07.090 --> 00:31:09.388
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:09.559 --> 00:31:12.255
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:12.428 --> 00:31:13.452
Fun.


00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:16.758
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:16.933 --> 00:31:20.334
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:21.204 --> 00:31:23.229
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:27.210 --> 00:31:29.576
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:29.913 --> 00:31:32.177
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:32.482 --> 00:31:35.576
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:35.852 --> 00:31:39.015
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:39.355 --> 00:31:42.415
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:42.592 --> 00:31:44.992
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:45.161 --> 00:31:48.096
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:48.264 --> 00:31:52.291
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:31:52.569 --> 00:31:55.868
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:31:57.073 --> 00:31:58.370
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:08.351 --> 00:32:10.615
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:10.787 --> 00:32:12.982
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:13.590 --> 00:32:16.616
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:17.794 --> 00:32:20.922
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:21.698 --> 00:32:23.962
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:24.133 --> 00:32:26.431
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:26.603 --> 00:32:29.800
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:33.009 --> 00:32:35.637
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:35.812 --> 00:32:38.872
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:39.048 --> 00:32:42.245
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:43.152 --> 00:32:46.019
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:46.189 --> 00:32:48.248
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:48.424 --> 00:32:49.516
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:50.126 --> 00:32:52.617
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:32:52.795 --> 00:32:54.262
...before Gail gets here.


00:32:54.998 --> 00:32:56.329
What about the demon spawn?


00:32:56.499 --> 00:32:57.523
Mm-hm.


00:32:57.700 --> 00:32:59.099
Right.


00:33:00.103 --> 00:33:01.502
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:04.574 --> 00:33:05.836
Hmm.


00:33:10.647 --> 00:33:12.638
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:13.316 --> 00:33:14.340
Ravi?


00:33:16.019 --> 00:33:18.544
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:18.721 --> 00:33:21.155
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:23.293 --> 00:33:25.853
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:26.029 --> 00:33:27.223
Obviously.


00:33:27.764 --> 00:33:30.255
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:30.433 --> 00:33:31.991
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:32.168 --> 00:33:35.535
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:36.072 --> 00:33:39.200
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:39.375 --> 00:33:42.037
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:42.412 --> 00:33:45.813
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:45.982 --> 00:33:47.847
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:48.217 --> 00:33:49.741
But I never got my shot.


00:33:49.919 --> 00:33:52.149
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:33:52.322 --> 00:33:54.722
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:33:54.891 --> 00:33:57.086
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:33:57.260 --> 00:33:58.750
"Who is asking?"


00:33:59.028 --> 00:34:02.395
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:02.565 --> 00:34:05.159
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:05.335 --> 00:34:09.704
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:10.006 --> 00:34:12.270
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:12.442 --> 00:34:14.842
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:15.178 --> 00:34:17.806
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:17.980 --> 00:34:19.174
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:20.383 --> 00:34:23.079
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:25.888 --> 00:34:29.551
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:30.226 --> 00:34:32.285
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:32.462 --> 00:34:34.930
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:35.098 --> 00:34:36.156
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:37.734 --> 00:34:39.065
Blow it up.


00:34:41.003 --> 00:34:42.561
Thank you.


00:34:52.382 --> 00:34:53.781
Whoa.


00:34:53.950 --> 00:34:56.578
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:34:56.753 --> 00:34:59.813
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:01.190 --> 00:35:03.522
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:03.693 --> 00:35:06.924
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:09.632 --> 00:35:12.601
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:12.769 --> 00:35:16.398
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:17.106 --> 00:35:19.438
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:24.814 --> 00:35:26.247
Where is he?


00:35:27.083 --> 00:35:29.881
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:30.052 --> 00:35:31.713
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:31.888 --> 00:35:34.322
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:37.827 --> 00:35:41.388
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:41.564 --> 00:35:44.897
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:45.067 --> 00:35:47.262
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:47.470 --> 00:35:50.200
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:50.373 --> 00:35:52.807
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:35:59.615 --> 00:36:00.673
I think I found him.


00:36:00.850 --> 00:36:03.114
Well, he is blond.


00:36:06.222 --> 00:36:08.520
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:10.426 --> 00:36:12.724
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:12.895 --> 00:36:14.294
What are you doing here?


00:36:14.464 --> 00:36:17.297
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.492
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:19.669 --> 00:36:22.604
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:22.772 --> 00:36:24.603
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:24.774 --> 00:36:27.242
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:29.679 --> 00:36:31.806
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:33.349 --> 00:36:36.785
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:36.953 --> 00:36:39.148
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:39.322 --> 00:36:42.189
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:42.358 --> 00:36:44.292
...and you're fired.


00:36:47.330 --> 00:36:50.857
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:36:53.469 --> 00:36:54.959
I heard you sing at school.


00:36:55.204 --> 00:36:56.330
You were amazing.


00:36:56.506 --> 00:36:57.564
Do I know you?


00:37:01.911 --> 00:37:04.505
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:06.849 --> 00:37:08.908
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:09.552 --> 00:37:12.043
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:16.559 --> 00:37:19.392
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:19.562 --> 00:37:20.927
Miss Van R.


00:37:21.564 --> 00:37:23.964
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:24.133 --> 00:37:25.327
...but were never good enough?


00:37:26.702 --> 00:37:28.363
Who told you that?


00:37:46.088 --> 00:37:47.521
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:47.690 --> 00:37:50.887
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:52.186
Oh!


00:37:52.361 --> 00:37:56.593
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:00.937 --> 00:38:04.031
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:04.206 --> 00:38:07.107
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:11.881 --> 00:38:14.611
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:14.951 --> 00:38:17.647
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:17.820 --> 00:38:19.082
Follow me.


00:38:24.126 --> 00:38:25.957
Oh, wow.


00:38:28.431 --> 00:38:33.994
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:34.870 --> 00:38:36.770
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:36.939 --> 00:38:40.636
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:42.144 --> 00:38:43.338
Or not.


00:38:45.615 --> 00:38:48.641
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:38:54.857 --> 00:38:58.418
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:38:59.729 --> 00:39:03.961
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:04.133 --> 00:39:07.660
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:07.837 --> 00:39:11.830
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:13.809 --> 00:39:17.142
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:18.914 --> 00:39:22.611
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:23.285 --> 00:39:26.982
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:27.456 --> 00:39:30.289
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:31.852
Uh-uh.


00:42:10.786 --> 00:42:13.380
I think I've blown something.


00:42:13.556 --> 00:42:16.616
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:19.228 --> 00:42:20.786
Move it, fatso.


00:42:22.531 --> 00:42:29.130
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:29.872 --> 00:42:33.501
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:46.055 --> 00:42:47.488
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:47.656 --> 00:42:49.681
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:49.859 --> 00:42:52.419
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:42:52.595 --> 00:42:54.563
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:42:57.032 --> 00:42:58.397
I'm so sorry.


00:42:59.101 --> 00:43:00.329
What...? You...?


00:43:01.036 --> 00:43:02.697
Hey. Wait.


00:43:02.872 --> 00:43:04.100
But who are you?


00:43:04.273 --> 00:43:06.867
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:15.017 --> 00:43:18.043
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:36.505 --> 00:43:38.530
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:39.308 --> 00:43:42.243
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:42.678 --> 00:43:45.613
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:45.948 --> 00:43:48.143
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:50.152 --> 00:43:53.315
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:43:53.489 --> 00:43:57.050
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:43:57.226 --> 00:43:59.490
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:43:59.662 --> 00:44:02.722
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:03.032 --> 00:44:06.160
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:07.069 --> 00:44:10.197
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:16.712 --> 00:44:19.943
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:20.115 --> 00:44:22.174
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:22.351 --> 00:44:24.285
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:24.453 --> 00:44:26.148
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:26.322 --> 00:44:28.620
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:29.992 --> 00:44:34.122
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:35.097 --> 00:44:38.692
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:39.768 --> 00:44:41.395
We're recording.


00:44:41.704 --> 00:44:43.535
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:43.706 --> 00:44:44.934
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:45.541 --> 00:44:47.475
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:47.643 --> 00:44:49.372
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:49.545 --> 00:44:51.877
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:44:52.047 --> 00:44:53.275
Check this out, all right?


00:44:53.449 --> 00:44:57.044
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:44:57.219 --> 00:44:59.050
...have music during the sixth period.


00:44:59.221 --> 00:45:01.052
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:01.256 --> 00:45:03.281
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:03.459 --> 00:45:04.619
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:04.793 --> 00:45:06.761
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:06.929 --> 00:45:08.794
That was subpar at best.


00:45:08.964 --> 00:45:11.489
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:12.234 --> 00:45:15.533
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:15.704 --> 00:45:17.262
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:17.439 --> 00:45:19.805
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:19.975 --> 00:45:23.001
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:23.178 --> 00:45:26.272
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:26.448 --> 00:45:28.006
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:28.450 --> 00:45:31.317
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:31.854 --> 00:45:35.415
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:35.691 --> 00:45:39.024
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:39.194 --> 00:45:41.788
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:41.964 --> 00:45:44.432
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:44.600 --> 00:45:47.694
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:47.870 --> 00:45:50.395
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:45:52.141 --> 00:45:56.737
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:45:56.912 --> 00:45:59.881
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:00.049 --> 00:46:02.882
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:08.924 --> 00:46:12.121
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:31.246 --> 00:46:33.544
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:33.715 --> 00:46:34.909
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:35.084 --> 00:46:37.382
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:37.553 --> 00:46:38.918
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:39.755 --> 00:46:41.882
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:42.057 --> 00:46:43.183
This is not good.


00:46:44.760 --> 00:46:46.557
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:46.728 --> 00:46:48.559
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:48.730 --> 00:46:51.130
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:51.300 --> 00:46:54.736
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:46:54.903 --> 00:46:55.927
Listen...


00:46:56.105 --> 00:46:59.541
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:46:59.708 --> 00:47:01.369
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:13.222 --> 00:47:17.215
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:17.392 --> 00:47:20.384
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:20.562 --> 00:47:24.191
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:24.366 --> 00:47:28.302
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:28.470 --> 00:47:32.270
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:32.808 --> 00:47:35.709
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:35.878 --> 00:47:38.938
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:40.749 --> 00:47:42.683
It was you?


00:47:43.352 --> 00:47:46.446
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:47.389 --> 00:47:51.223
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:47:52.861 --> 00:47:55.887
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:47:56.064 --> 00:47:58.828
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:47:59.001 --> 00:48:01.128
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:01.770 --> 00:48:04.500
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:04.773 --> 00:48:06.536
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:06.708 --> 00:48:10.075
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:10.245 --> 00:48:12.509
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:14.016 --> 00:48:15.813
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:15.984 --> 00:48:17.076
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:18.020 --> 00:48:19.487
You have a date with detention.


00:48:19.655 --> 00:48:21.122
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:21.290 --> 00:48:23.019
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:23.192 --> 00:48:25.888
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:26.061 --> 00:48:29.189
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:29.364 --> 00:48:30.854
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:31.033 --> 00:48:32.933
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:33.101 --> 00:48:35.899
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:36.071 --> 00:48:38.437
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:38.607 --> 00:48:40.074
Fine.


00:48:40.876 --> 00:48:42.400
I hate you.


00:48:46.048 --> 00:48:50.178
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:50.452 --> 00:48:52.386
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:48:58.961 --> 00:49:00.588
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:00.762 --> 00:49:03.959
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:04.132 --> 00:49:05.599
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:05.767 --> 00:49:08.565
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:08.737 --> 00:49:10.932
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


